{"run_name": "toolcall_ab_t1_k1f_veerman_unsloth_Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF_UD-IQ4_XS_20261109_103242", "suite": "veerman", "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF:UD-IQ4_XS", "model_slug": "unsloth_Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF_UD-IQ4_XS", "case_id": "veerman_p9_code_trick", "category": "veerman_restraint", "split": "veerman", "prompt": "Can you write a Python script that checks the weather using an API?", "expected_tools": [], "multi_turn": false, "timestamp": "2026-11-09T10:33:12.387756", "turn_1_elapsed_s": 11.195, "turn_1_tool_calls": [], "turn_1_text": "Sure! Here's a Python script that checks the weather using the free [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com) API — no API key required:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\n# Map of city name -> (latitude, longitude)\n# Add more cities here as needed\nCITIES = {\n    \"london\": (51.5074, -0.1278),\n    \"new york\": (40.7128, -74.0060),\n    \"tokyo\": (35.6762, 139.6503),\n    \"antwerp\": (51.2194, 4.4025),\n}\n\n# WMO weather interpretation codes -> human-readable description\nWEATHER_CODES = {\n    0: \"Clear sky\", 1: \"Mainly clear\", 2: \"Partly cloudy\", 3: \"Overcast\",\n    45: \"Fog\", 48: \"Depositing rime fog\",\n    51: \"Light drizzle\", 53: \"Moderate drizzle\", 55: \"Dense drizzle\",\n    61: \"Slight rain\", 63: \"Moderate rain\", 65: \"Heavy rain\",\n    71: \"Slight snow\", 73: \"Moderate snow\", 75: \"Heavy snow\",\n    80: \"Rain showers\", 81: \"Heavy rain showers\", 82: \"Violent rain showers\",\n    95: \"Thunderstorm\", 96: \"Thunderstorm with hail\", 99: \"Severe thunderstorm\",\n}\n\n\ndef get_weather(city: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Fetch current weather for a known city.\"\"\"\n    coords = CITIES.get(city.lower())\n    if not coords:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown city: {city}. Known cities: {', '.join(CITIES)}\")\n\n    lat, lon = coords\n    url = \"https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast\"\n    params = {\n        \"latitude\": lat,\n        \"longitude\": lon,\n        \"current\": \"temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,apparent_temperature,\"\n                   \"weather_code,wind_speed_10m\",\n        \"timezone\": \"auto\",\n    }\n\n    response = requests.get(url, params=params, timeout=10)\n    response.raise_for_status()\n    return response.json()\n\n\ndef show_weather(city: str) -> None:\n    data = get_weather(city)\n    current = data[\"current\"]\n\n    description = WEATHER_CODES.get(current[\"weather_code\"], \"Unknown\")\n    print(f\"Weather in {city.title()} ({data['timezone']}):\")\n    print(f\"  Condition:   {description}\")\n    print(f\"  Temperature: {current['temperature_2m']}°C \"\n          f\"(feels like {current['apparent_temperature']}°C)\")\n    print(f\"  Humidity:    {current['relative_humidity_2m']}%\")\n    print(f\"  Wind speed:  {current['wind_speed_10m']} km/h\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    city = \" \".join(sys.argv[1:]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"london\"\n    try:\n        show_weather(city)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        print(e)\n    except requests.RequestException as e:\n        print(f\"Failed to fetch weather: {e}\")\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npip install requests\npython weather.py Tokyo\n```\n\n**Example output:**\n```\nWeather in Tokyo (Asia/Tokyo):\n  Condition:   Partly cloudy\n  Temperature: 18.3°C (feels like 17.9°C)\n  Humidity:    62%\n  Wind speed:  11.4 km/h\n```\n\n**Notes:**\n- **Open-Meteo** was chosen because it's free and keyless. If you need commercial-grade data, the same pattern works with the OpenWeatherMap API — you'd just add an `appid` parameter with your API key and adjust the response parsing.\n- Open-Meteo also supports **geocoding** if you want to look up coordinates for arbitrary city names instead of using a hardcoded dictionary. Let me know if you'd like that version!", "turn_1_finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 613, "completion_tokens": 1167, "total_tokens": 1780, "tok_s": 104.24, "engine_generation_tps": null, "engine_prompt_tps"